    pr_ref:  # 7f16
    description: "PR #689 (WI-fagit) retargets C# 'new X(...)' instantiation edges to the constructor node via the Type.Type key, but register_symbol keys the global registry by name, so overloaded constructors (all named Type.Type) collapse to the last-registered one. Every 'new X(...)' of an overloaded type therefore shares one ctor anchor; a reverse-slice on a NON-last overload still misses its callers. Single-ctor classes (the dominant case) are fully correct. Fix: build a class->[ctors] multi-map (like global_methods) and match the object_creation_expression's argument count against each ctor's parameter count; fall back to the first ctor on no arity match."  # 7f16
    fields: {}  # 7f16
