- op: discuss  # 8e01
  at: '2026-07-28T05:08:18Z'  # 8e01
  by: agent  # 8e01
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8e01
  clock: 3  # 8e01
  nonce: '8e01'  # 8e01
  message: "PR #45 (dev 2a2fb48463): fixed. new X(...) no longer collapses onto the last-registered ctor — the C# analyzer builds a global_ctors multi-map (parallel to global_methods) and binds the instantiates edge to the overload whose parameter count matches the arg count. Behavioral evidence: test_overloaded_ctor_resolves_by_arity (production path) — two overloaded Widget ctors (1-arg/2-arg), each new Widget(...) now targets its arity-matching ctor node (before: both collapsed onto the 2-arg ctor). Scope: arity-precise matching as filed; exact param==arg count, optional/params args not modeled and SAME-arity overloads (Foo(int) vs Foo(string)) still fall back to the collapsed pick — full type-based C# overload resolution is out of scope. Object-initializer new X { } (no arglist) falls back gracefully (tested)."  # 8e01
